      <div itemprop="text">
        <p>No. Xreader is Linux Mint's PDF, PostScript, DjVu, XPS, and comics viewer, which has been part of XApp for years. Xepub is a separate, EPUB-only application built specifically for reflowable content. They ship side-by-side on Linux Mint: open an EPUB in Xepub, open a PDF in Xreader.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
