        <p>No. Xepub reads DRM-free EPUB files only. For Adobe Digital Editions EPUB or LCP-protected library loans, use Thorium Reader (EDRLab), which is the only Linux-native reader with LCP support as of September 2026. Most public-library ebooks can also be sideloaded directly to a Kobo via Libby.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
