        <p>No, and it isn't trying to. Xepub is a reader, not a library manager. Calibre still owns format conversion (EPUB ↔ MOBI ↔ AZW3 ↔ DOCX), metadata editing, cover generation, and direct device sideloading. On Linux Mint, the natural pairing is Calibre for library work and Xepub for day-to-day reading.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
